# Normalize line endings so Windows checkouts always store LF in git,
# regardless of any single machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# any editor/tool that saves a file with CRLF on Windows makes git see
# every line in that file as "changed" on the next diff/merge/pull, even
# when the actual text content is identical — which is what was causing
# every recent merge in this repo to look far messier than it really was.
* text=auto eol=lf
